    "title": "From Haverford High to Olympic gold, world records and a memorable feat - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Editorials ,\n10 hours ago As the 1932 Summer Olympics in Los Angeles approached, Jean Shiley and Babe Didrikson were America’s favorites in the women’s high jump event, with Shiley, the American record holder. At the AAU National Championships that year, which also served as the Olympic trials, Shiley tied the legendary Didrikson with a world record jump of 5 feet 3 3/16 inches. Read full article",
